WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.183
Look up at the Moon tonight, and again
next week. It will look different.

2
00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:12.840
It is the same ball of rock all
month, going round the Earth.

3
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.776
The Earth, the Sun and the
Moon are all shaped like balls.

4
00:00:16.996 --> 00:00:20.804
A ball shape is called a sphere.
So all three are spheres.

5
00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:26.040
The Sun is a huge ball of hot, glowing
gas. Never look straight at it.

6
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.300
The Earth looks flat from where
you stand, because it is so big.

7
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.282
From space it is a round
blue ball, not a flat plate.

8
00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:38.265
Look at the Moon night after
night, and it seems to change.

9
00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:42.339
It starts as a new Moon.
The side facing us is dark.

10
00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:46.553
Then a thin crescent, then a
half Moon, then a full circle.

11
00:00:46.773 --> 00:00:50.860
Growing is called waxing. Shrinking
back down is called waning.

12
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.981
The whole pattern takes about four
weeks, and then it starts again.

13
00:00:55.481 --> 00:00:59.753
The Moon does not really change
shape. It is always a ball.

14
00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:04.989
Make a model with a grown-up: a lamp
in a dark room, and a ball on a stick.

15
00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:10.457
The lamp is the Sun. It lights one half of
the ball, and the other half stays dark.

16
00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:15.599
Your head is the Earth. Hold the
ball up, and turn slowly on the spot.

17
00:01:15.819 --> 00:01:19.534
You see a thin crescent, then a
half, then the whole lit face.

18
00:01:19.754 --> 00:01:24.816
The ball never changed shape. Only how
much of its lit half you could see.

19
00:01:25.316 --> 00:01:29.821
The Moon travels round the Earth.
That path is called its orbit.

20
00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:33.756
One trip round takes about
four weeks: a month, not a day.

21
00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:37.413
The Earth itself spins on
the spot, once every day.

22
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:41.580
That spin is what gives us
day and night, over and over.

23
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.469
Today you will build this model
on screen, and make it move.

24
00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:50.102
Long ago, many people thought
the Earth was flat, like a plate.

25
00:01:50.322 --> 00:01:54.269
They watched the Sun cross the
sky and thought it went round us.

26
00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:58.251
Then telescopes showed the Moon
is a rocky ball, with craters.

27
00:01:58.471 --> 00:02:02.976
In 1969 astronauts stood on the
Moon and photographed the Earth.

28
00:02:03.196 --> 00:02:06.539
Science changes when
people look more carefully.

29
00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:10.801
The Earth, the Sun and the Moon
are all spheres: ball shapes.

30
00:02:11.021 --> 00:02:17.058
The phases go new, crescent, half, full,
and back to new. It is always a ball.

31
00:02:17.278 --> 00:02:21.133
It goes round the Earth in a
month. The Earth spins once a day.

32
00:02:21.353 --> 00:02:24.511
And our ideas change when
we look more carefully.
